{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 103.77.2.19 attempted a Path Traversal attack by injecting directory traversal sequences (such as '../' and its URL-encoded or backslash variants) into the parameters of various endpoints like '/download', '/img', and '/static/'. These attempts aimed to access sensitive system files such as '/etc/passwd', '/etc/shadow', and 'win.ini'. The HTTP 403 status codes indicate that the web server successfully blocked these requests.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement strict input validation and allowlisting for parameters that handle file paths or names.",
    "Use built-in framework functions or libraries designed to safely resolve file paths and prevent directory traversal (e.g., canonicalization).",
    "Ensure the web application runs with the principle of least privilege, restricting read permissions on sensitive system files."
  ]
}
